enum users_role {
  non_validated
  member
  moderator
  admin
  /// The operator of the whole deployment, not of one community. Only ever
  /// held on the root tenant (SystemAdminGuard checks both the role and
  /// `req.tenant.isRoot`), and it is the role that manages tenants.
  ///
  /// RolesGuard treats it as satisfying @Roles(ADMIN), so the system admin
  /// keeps every ordinary admin capability on the root tenant rather than
  /// needing a second account. See the hierarchy note in roles.guard.ts.
  system_admin
  automation
  /// Holds no privileges at all. RolesGuard is an allowlist, so a `disabled`
  /// account matches no @Roles() and can reach nothing role-gated.
  ///
  /// Carried by the service account every non-root tenant gets: those tenants
  /// have no automation to run, and giving them a real `automation` role would
  /// hand every tenant admin an escalation path -- admin.service.setRole lets
  /// an `automation` account be promoted to admin on purpose (see the note
  /// there), and that exception is only safe on the tenant the operator owns.
  disabled
}

